+# Aegis Level‑4 Readiness Scorecard
+
+Purpose
+- Provide a measurable checklist and scoring rubric for Level‑4 readiness. Use this to track progress and focus remediation.
+
+How to use
+- For each item, mark: ✅ (done), ⚠️ (partial/unstable), ❌ (missing).
+- Weighted score is provided. Total score >= 90% indicates readiness to request external audit.
+
+Scoring weights (total 100):
+- Integration & evidence (30)
+- Identity & governance (15)
+- DP accounting & FL integration (15)
+- MPC production hardening (15)
+- KMS/HSM & key lifecycle (10)
+- Observability & SLOs (8)
+- Runbooks & drills (7)
+
+Checklist
+1) Integration & evidence (30)
+ - [ ] Flagger -> canary-signing post-rollout webhook configured and verified (5)
+ - [ ] Every autonomous decision produces a signed manifest and Rekor entry (10)
+ - [ ] Evidence S3 bucket versioning & lifecycle configured (5)
+ - [ ] Hardened deploy pipeline verifies cosign + Rekor before deploy (10)
+
+2) Identity & governance (15)
+ - [ ] M‑of‑N service deployed + OIDC jwks configured (6)
+ - [ ] CI PR gates enforce MOFN approval for high-risk PRs (5)
+ - [ ] Approver list & rotation policy documented (4)
+
+3) DP accounting & FL integration (15)
+ - [ ] FL controller calls /check_run before each round (7)
+ - [ ] FL controller calls /report_round after each round (4)
+ - [ ] Opacus RDP accountant integration tested on representative dataset (4)
+
+4) MPC production hardening (15)
+ - [ ] Multi-host MPC deployed in staging with mTLS (4)
+ - [ ] Malicious‑share tests exist and pass (5)
+ - [ ] Streaming/chunking implemented for large tensors (3)
+ - [ ] External crypto audit scheduled (3)
+
+5) KMS/HSM & key lifecycle (10)
+ - [ ] KMS alias rotation produces signed manifest (4)
+ - [ ] Alias swap gated by M‑of‑N or manual approval (3)
+ - [ ] Rekor registered for key rotation manifests (3)
+
+6) Observability & SLOs (8)
+ - [ ] Prometheus rules for SLOs in repo and imported in staging (3)
+ - [ ] Grafana dashboards provisioned & validated (3)
+ - [ ] Alertmanager rules for safety signals (1)
+ - [ ] Runbook responders' contact info in runbook (1)
+
+7) Runbooks & drills (7)
+ - [ ] Weekly runbook drill scheduled + GH action exists (3)
+ - [ ] Drill artifacts archived & accessible (2)
+ - [ ] Post‑drill reviews and tickets created (2)
+
+Scoring example
+- For each checked item, add weight. Compute percent.
+- Use ops/orchestrator/one_click_orchestrator.sh to run drills and collect artifacts for scoring.
+
+Next steps
+- Run the Scorecard Runner script (ops/ci/scorecard_runner.py) to auto-evaluate many items and produce a preliminary score.
