*** Add File:ops/secure_agg/production_mpc/streaming_protocol.md
+Streaming & chunking protocol notes (for large model vectors)
+
+1) Motivation
+ - Large model vectors (millions of elements) cannot be secret-shared or encrypted in a single message without high memory overhead; stream/ chunk to reduce memory.
+
+2) Client-side
+ - Quantize floats -> int32/int64
+ - Split vector into N chunks of size <= MAX_CHUNK_SIZE
+ - For each chunk:
+    - Create secret shares using threshold scheme
+    - Send share metadata (vector id, chunk id, total chunks, share id)
+
+3) Aggregator-side
+ - Validate chunk headers (vector id, chunk id continuity)
+ - Temporarily store per-chunk shares; only attempt reconstruction once k shares are present
+ - Reconstruct chunk in-memory and accumulate into running sum (use streaming addition)
+ - Delete shares after reconstruction to avoid retention and limit attack surface
+
+4) Security considerations
+ - Use mTLS for client->aggregator transport
+ - Rate-limit and authenticate clients
+ - Keep chunk size small enough to avoid OOM but large enough to reduce request overhead
+ - Use HMAC/nonce per chunk to prevent replay
+
